IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb5-nouns`
IMPORT `cb5-part19-1-damages`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), RELATED PROVISIONS (src:3543-3604).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Nothing here takes anyone's point of view.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice
-- Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version,
-- and nothing here has been verified against the official text. Contains information licensed under
-- the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS. The Related Provisions are provisions of amending Acts that stay in force beside the
-- Act: transitional rules, time limits for continuance, reviews. Each is encoded as the Act's text puts it.
--
-- DATES. The text of the Related Provisions never states the day an amending Act, a section or a Part
-- "comes into force", or the day it was "assented to". Each such day is a plain DATE input named for the
-- event, and no calendar date is invented. The dates of the Act's own text (the consolidation date above)
-- are not used by any rule.

§ `Related provisions`

§§ `S.C. 2001, c. 14, s. 233 -- Part XIX.1 and proceedings begun before it`

-- "Does not apply to any proceeding commenced before the coming into force of that section" (section 115 of
-- the 2001 Act, which enacted Part XIX.1). A proceeding commenced on the very day is not commenced before it.
-- src:3577 | 233 Part XIX.1 of the Canada Business Corporations Act, as enacted by section 115 of this Act, does not apply to any proceeding commenced before the coming into force of that section.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 2001, c. 14, s. 233 (src:3577)
GIVEN `the day the proceeding was commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day section 115 of S.C. 2001, c. 14 came into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part XIX.1 applies to the proceeding within S.C. 2001, c. 14, s. 233` IF
    `the day the proceeding was commenced` AT LEAST `the day section 115 of S.C. 2001, c. 14 came into force`

-- The whole question "does Part XIX.1 govern this apportionment": s 237.2(1) is met, s 237.2(2) does not
-- exclude the plaintiff, and the transitional section lets the Part reach the proceeding.
-- src:3577 | 233 Part XIX.1 of the Canada Business Corporations Act, as enacted by section 115 of this Act, does not apply to any proceeding commenced before the coming into force of that section.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 2001, c. 14, s. 233 (src:3577)
GIVEN `damages are awarded to a plaintiff for financial loss` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of defendants and third parties the court has found responsible for the financial loss` IS A NUMBER
      kind IS A `Kind of plaintiff (s 237.2(2))`
      `a substantial part of the activities of the plaintiff involves trading, including making investments in, securities or other financial instruments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the proceeding was commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day section 115 of S.C. 2001, c. 14 came into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part XIX.1 governs the apportionment of the damages` IF
        `Part XIX.1 applies to the apportionment within s 237.2(1)` `damages are awarded to a plaintiff for financial loss` `the number of defendants and third parties the court has found responsible for the financial loss`
    AND (NOT `Part XIX.1 does not apply to the plaintiff within s 237.2(2)` kind `a substantial part of the activities of the plaintiff involves trading, including making investments in, securities or other financial instruments`)
    AND `Part XIX.1 applies to the proceeding within S.C. 2001, c. 14, s. 233` `the day the proceeding was commenced` `the day section 115 of S.C. 2001, c. 14 came into force`

§§ `R.S. 1985, c. 27 (2nd Supp.), s. 11; S.C. 1990, c. 17, s. 45(1); S.C. 1998, c. 30, s. 10 -- proceedings begun before an amendment`

-- Each of the three says that a proceeding commenced before the coming into force of the amending section,
-- to which an amended provision applies, is taken up and continued under that amended provision without
-- further formality. The amended provisions are not named in the Act's text; the question is only whether the
-- proceeding is continued under them.
-- src:3547 | 11 Proceedings to which any of the provisions amended by the schedule apply that were commenced before the coming into force of section 10 shall be continued in accordance with those amended provisions without any further formality.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, R.S. 1985, c. 27 (2nd Supp.), s. 11 (src:3547)
GIVEN `the day the proceeding was commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day section 10 of R.S. 1985, c. 27 (2nd Supp.) came into force` IS A DATE
      `a provision amended by the schedule to that Act applies to the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proceeding is continued in accordance with the amended provisions within R.S. 1985, c. 27 (2nd Supp.), s. 11` IF
        `the day the proceeding was commenced` LESS THAN `the day section 10 of R.S. 1985, c. 27 (2nd Supp.) came into force`
    AND `a provision amended by the schedule to that Act applies to the proceeding`

-- src:3551 | 45 (1) Every proceeding commenced before the coming into force of this subsection and in respect of which any provision amended by this Act applies shall be taken up and continued under and in conformity with that amended provision without any further formality.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 1990, c. 17, s. 45(1) (src:3551)
GIVEN `the day the proceeding was commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day subsection 45(1) of S.C. 1990, c. 17 came into force` IS A DATE
      `a provision amended by that Act applies to the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proceeding is taken up and continued under the amended provision within S.C. 1990, c. 17, s. 45(1)` IF
        `the day the proceeding was commenced` LESS THAN `the day subsection 45(1) of S.C. 1990, c. 17 came into force`
    AND `a provision amended by that Act applies to the proceeding`

-- src:3570 | 10 Every proceeding commenced before the coming into force of this section and in respect of which any provision amended by sections 12 to 16 applies shall be taken up and continued under and in conformity with that amended provision without any further formality.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 1998, c. 30, s. 10 (src:3570)
GIVEN `the day the proceeding was commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day section 10 of S.C. 1998, c. 30 came into force` IS A DATE
      `a provision amended by sections 12 to 16 of that Act applies to the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proceeding is taken up and continued under the amended provision within S.C. 1998, c. 30, s. 10` IF
        `the day the proceeding was commenced` LESS THAN `the day section 10 of S.C. 1998, c. 30 came into force`
    AND `a provision amended by sections 12 to 16 of that Act applies to the proceeding`

§§ `S.C. 1994, c. 21, s. 125(2) -- subsection (1) applies after 1988`

-- "Subsection (1) applies after 1988." Subsection (1) is not in the Act's text, and "after 1988" is read as
-- the years from 1989 on, the year being the calendar year (fork F-125(2)-1 in NOTES.md).
-- src:3554 | 125 (2) Subsection (1) applies after 1988.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 1994, c. 21, s. 125(2) (src:3554)
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsection 125(1) applies to the year within S.C. 1994, c. 21, s. 125(2)` IF
    `the year` GREATER THAN 1988

§§ `S.C. 1994, c. 24, s. 33; S.C. 2001, c. 14, s. 136; S.C. 2018, c. 8, s. 107.1 -- reviews of the Act`

-- 1994 c 24 s 33(1): within three years after the day the Act is assented to, the Minister causes a report to
-- be laid before both Houses.
-- src:3558 | 33 (1) Within three years after the day on which this Act is assented to, the Minister shall cause to be laid before both Houses of Parliament a report on the provisions and operation of the Canada Business Corporations Act, including any recommendations for amendments to that Act.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 1994, c. 24, s. 33(1) (src:3558)
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`the period for the Minister to lay the report within S.C. 1994, c. 24, s. 33(1)` MEANS
    `Time limit` WITH
        `number of units` IS 3
        `unit of time` IS `calendar years`

-- src:3558 | 33 (1) Within three years after the day on which this Act is assented to, the Minister shall cause to be laid before both Houses of Parliament a report on the provisions and operation of the Canada Business Corporations Act, including any recommendations for amendments to that Act.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 1994, c. 24, s. 33(1) (src:3558)
GIVEN `the day the Act was assented to` IS A DATE
      `the day the report was laid before both Houses` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister has laid the report in time within S.C. 1994, c. 24, s. 33(1)` IF
    `done within the time limit` `the period for the Minister to lay the report within S.C. 1994, c. 24, s. 33(1)` `the day the Act was assented to` `the day the report was laid before both Houses`

-- (2)(a): the committee reviews the report "as soon as possible thereafter": the duty arises once the report
-- stands referred to it.
-- src:3560 | (2) The report stands referred to the committee of the House of Commons, or of both Houses of Parliament, that is designated or established for that purpose, which shall
-- src:3561 | (a) as soon as possible thereafter review the report and undertake a comprehensive review of the provisions and operation of the Canada Business Corporations Act; and
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 1994, c. 24, s. 33(2)(a) (src:3560-3561)
GIVEN `the report stands referred to the committee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the committee must review the report and the Act as soon as possible within S.C. 1994, c. 24, s. 33(2)(a)` IF
    `the report stands referred to the committee`

-- (2)(b): the committee reports within one year after the laying of the Minister's report, "or any further
-- time that the House of Commons, or both Houses of Parliament, may authorize": the later of the two days.
-- src:3562 | (b) report to the House of Commons, or to both Houses of Parliament, within one year after the laying of the report of the Minister or any further time that the House of Commons, or both Houses of Parliament, may authorize.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 1994, c. 24, s. 33(2)(b) (src:3562)
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`the period for the committee to report within S.C. 1994, c. 24, s. 33(2)(b)` MEANS
    `Time limit` WITH
        `number of units` IS 1
        `unit of time` IS `calendar years`

-- src:3562 | (b) report to the House of Commons, or to both Houses of Parliament, within one year after the laying of the report of the Minister or any further time that the House of Commons, or both Houses of Parliament, may authorize.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 1994, c. 24, s. 33(2)(b) (src:3562)
GIVEN `the day the Minister's report was laid` IS A DATE
      `the last day of any further time authorized` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day for the committee to report within S.C. 1994, c. 24, s. 33(2)(b)` IS
    CONSIDER `the last day of any further time authorized`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the last day of` `the period for the committee to report within S.C. 1994, c. 24, s. 33(2)(b)` `counted from` `the day the Minister's report was laid`
    WHEN JUST d THEN IF d GREATER THAN `the last day of` `the period for the committee to report within S.C. 1994, c. 24, s. 33(2)(b)` `counted from` `the day the Minister's report was laid`
                     THEN d
                     ELSE `the last day of` `the period for the committee to report within S.C. 1994, c. 24, s. 33(2)(b)` `counted from` `the day the Minister's report was laid`

-- 2001 c 14 s 136: within five years after the coming into force of the section, and within every ten years
-- thereafter, a review. The nth review is due n-1 ten-year periods after the first five years, counted from
-- the coming into force (fork F-136-1 in NOTES.md: the ten years run from the previous due day, not from the
-- day the previous review was in fact finished).
-- src:3574 | 136 A committee of the Senate, of the House of Commons or of both Houses of Parliament that is designated or established for the purpose shall, within five years after the coming into force of this section, and within every ten years thereafter, undertake a review of the provisions and operations of the Canada Business Corporations Act, and shall, within a reasonable period thereafter, cause to be laid before each House of Parliament a report thereon.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 2001, c. 14, s. 136 (src:3574)
GIVEN `the day section 136 of S.C. 2001, c. 14 came into force` IS A DATE
      `which review it is, counting the first as 1` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day for the review within S.C. 2001, c. 14, s. 136` IS
    `add years` `the day section 136 of S.C. 2001, c. 14 came into force` (5 PLUS (10 TIMES (`which review it is, counting the first as 1` MINUS 1)))

-- "Within a reasonable period thereafter, cause to be laid before each House a report": no fixed time, so
-- the answer is only whether the duty has arisen.
-- src:3574 | 136 A committee of the Senate, of the House of Commons or of both Houses of Parliament that is designated or established for the purpose shall, within five years after the coming into force of this section, and within every ten years thereafter, undertake a review of the provisions and operations of the Canada Business Corporations Act, and shall, within a reasonable period thereafter, cause to be laid before each House of Parliament a report thereon.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 2001, c. 14, s. 136 (src:3574)
GIVEN `a review has been undertaken` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the committee must cause a report to be laid before each House within a reasonable period within S.C. 2001, c. 14, s. 136` IF
    `a review has been undertaken`

-- 2018 c 8 s 107.1(1): on the fifth anniversary of the day section 24 comes into force, the provisions under
-- Part XIV.1 are referred to a committee.
-- src:3602 | 107.1 (1) On the fifth anniversary of the day on which section 24 of this Act comes into force, the provisions under Part XIV.1 of the Canada Business Corporations Act are to be referred to a committee of the Senate, of the House of Commons or of both Houses of Parliament that may be designated or established for the purpose of reviewing those provisions.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 2018, c. 8, s. 107.1(1) (src:3602)
GIVEN `the day section 24 of S.C. 2018, c. 8 came into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the day Part XIV.1 is to be referred to a committee within S.C. 2018, c. 8, s. 107.1(1)` IS
    `add years` `the day section 24 of S.C. 2018, c. 8 came into force` 5

-- src:3604 | (2) The committee referred to in subsection (1) shall, within a reasonable time after a review is completed, submit a report on that review to the Senate, the House of Commons or both Houses of Parliament, as the case may be.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 2018, c. 8, s. 107.1(2) (src:3604)
GIVEN `a review of Part XIV.1 has been completed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the committee must submit a report within a reasonable time within S.C. 2018, c. 8, s. 107.1(2)` IF
    `a review of Part XIV.1 has been completed`

§§ `S.C. 1996, c. 10, s. 214 -- previous continuance of railway companies`

-- "No continuance of a railway company granted under section 187 ... before section 212 comes into force is
-- invalid because the company was incorporated by or under an Act of Parliament." The rule says whether the
-- continuance is saved from that ground of invalidity: it was a railway company's, granted under section 187
-- before the day section 212 came into force.
-- src:3566 | 214 No continuance of a railway company granted under section 187 of the Canada Business Corporations Act before section 212 comes into force is invalid because the company was incorporated by or under an Act of Parliament.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 1996, c. 10, s. 214 (src:3566)
GIVEN `the continuance was of a railway company and was granted under section 187` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the continuance was granted` IS A DATE
      `the day section 212 of S.C. 1996, c. 10 came into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the continuance is not invalid because the company was incorporated by or under an Act of Parliament within S.C. 1996, c. 10, s. 214` IF
        `the continuance was of a railway company and was granted under section 187`
    AND `the day the continuance was granted` LESS THAN `the day section 212 of S.C. 1996, c. 10 came into force`

§§ `S.C. 2009, c. 23, s. 297(6) -- six months to continue, or dissolved`

-- A body corporate referred to in subsection 297(2) of that Act (a body under the Canada Corporations Act;
-- the 2009 Act is not among the sources) that does not apply for a certificate of continuance under section
-- 187 within six months after the day the subsection comes into force "is dissolved on the expiry of that
-- period", despite the Canada Corporations Act.
-- src:3581 | 297 (6) Despite any provision of the Canada Corporations Act, a body corporate referred to in subsection (2) that does not apply for a certificate of continuance under section 187 of the Canada Business Corporations Act within six months after the day on which this subsection comes into force is dissolved on the expiry of that period.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 2009, c. 23, s. 297(6) (src:3581)
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`the period to apply for continuance within S.C. 2009, c. 23, s. 297(6)` MEANS
    `Time limit` WITH
        `number of units` IS 6
        `unit of time` IS `calendar months`

-- src:3581 | 297 (6) Despite any provision of the Canada Corporations Act, a body corporate referred to in subsection (2) that does not apply for a certificate of continuance under section 187 of the Canada Business Corporations Act within six months after the day on which this subsection comes into force is dissolved on the expiry of that period.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 2009, c. 23, s. 297(6) (src:3581)
GIVEN `the day subsection 297(6) of S.C. 2009, c. 23 came into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day to apply for continuance within S.C. 2009, c. 23, s. 297(6)` IS
    `the last day of` `the period to apply for continuance within S.C. 2009, c. 23, s. 297(6)` `counted from` `the day subsection 297(6) of S.C. 2009, c. 23 came into force`

-- src:3581 | 297 (6) Despite any provision of the Canada Corporations Act, a body corporate referred to in subsection (2) that does not apply for a certificate of continuance under section 187 of the Canada Business Corporations Act within six months after the day on which this subsection comes into force is dissolved on the expiry of that period.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 2009, c. 23, s. 297(6) (src:3581)
GIVEN `the body corporate is one referred to in subsection 297(2) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day subsection 297(6) of S.C. 2009, c. 23 came into force` IS A DATE
      `the day the body corporate applied for a certificate of continuance under section 187` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day it is asked whether the body corporate is dissolved` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body corporate is dissolved on the expiry of the period within S.C. 2009, c. 23, s. 297(6)` IF
        `the body corporate is one referred to in subsection 297(2) of that Act`
    AND (CONSIDER `the day the body corporate applied for a certificate of continuance under section 187`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST a THEN (NOT `done within the time limit` `the period to apply for continuance within S.C. 2009, c. 23, s. 297(6)` `the day subsection 297(6) of S.C. 2009, c. 23 came into force` a))
    AND `the day it is asked whether the body corporate is dissolved` GREATER THAN `the last day to apply for continuance within S.C. 2009, c. 23, s. 297(6)` `the day subsection 297(6) of S.C. 2009, c. 23 came into force`

§§ `S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42 -- the Corporation's application for continuance`

-- The "Corporation" is the one the Part of the 2011 Act is about; its name is not in the Act's text.
-- (1): the application is for continuance under one of three Acts, and is for the Minister's approval.
-- src:3585 | 42 (1) The Corporation must submit an application for continuance under one of the following Acts for the Minister’s approval:
-- src:3586 | (a) the Canada Business Corporations Act;
-- src:3587 | (b) the Canada Cooperatives Act; or
-- src:3588 | (c) the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(1) (src:3585-3588)
DECLARE `Act of continuance (S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(1))` IS ONE OF
    `the Canada Business Corporations Act (S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(1)(a))`
    `the Canada Cooperatives Act (S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(1)(b))`
    `the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act (S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(1)(c))`
    `another Act (S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(1))`

-- src:3585 | 42 (1) The Corporation must submit an application for continuance under one of the following Acts for the Minister’s approval:
-- src:3586 | (a) the Canada Business Corporations Act;
-- src:3587 | (b) the Canada Cooperatives Act; or
-- src:3588 | (c) the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(1) (src:3585-3588)
GIVEN act IS A `Act of continuance (S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(1))`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation may submit an application for continuance under the Act for the Minister's approval within S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(1)` IF
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `the Canada Business Corporations Act (S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(1)(a))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Canada Cooperatives Act (S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(1)(b))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Canada Not-for-profit Corporations Act (S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(1)(c))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another Act (S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(1))` THEN FALSE

-- (2): within four years, or any shorter period the Minister specifies, after the day the Part comes into
-- force: the earlier of the two days.
-- src:3590 | (2) The application must be submitted to the Minister within four years, or any shorter period specified by the Minister, after the day on which this Part comes into force.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(2) (src:3590)
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`the period of four years within S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(2)` MEANS
    `Time limit` WITH
        `number of units` IS 4
        `unit of time` IS `calendar years`

-- src:3590 | (2) The application must be submitted to the Minister within four years, or any shorter period specified by the Minister, after the day on which this Part comes into force.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(2) (src:3590)
GIVEN `the day the Part comes into force` IS A DATE
      `the number of days in any shorter period specified by the Minister` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the last day to submit the application to the Minister within S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(2)` IS
    CONSIDER `the number of days in any shorter period specified by the Minister`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the last day of` `the period of four years within S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(2)` `counted from` `the day the Part comes into force`
    WHEN JUST n THEN IF `the day the Part comes into force` PLUS n LESS THAN `the last day of` `the period of four years within S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(2)` `counted from` `the day the Part comes into force`
                     THEN `the day the Part comes into force` PLUS n
                     ELSE `the last day of` `the period of four years within S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(2)` `counted from` `the day the Part comes into force`

-- (3): once the Minister approves, the Corporation submits the application to the applicable authorities.
-- src:3592 | (3) Once the application has been approved by the Minister, the Corporation must submit the application to the applicable authorities under the relevant Act.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(3) (src:3592)
GIVEN `the Minister has approved the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation must submit the application to the applicable authorities within S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(3)` IF
    `the Minister has approved the application`

-- (4): "not invalid solely because": the one ground, being incorporated by an Act of Parliament, does not by
-- itself invalidate it.
-- src:3594 | (4) The application is not invalid solely because the Corporation is incorporated by an Act of Parliament.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(4) (src:3594)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the application is invalid solely because the Corporation is incorporated by an Act of Parliament within S.C. 2011, c. 25, s. 42(4)` MEANS FALSE

§§ `S.C. 2012, c. 19, s. 210 -- PPP Canada Inc.`

-- "Except as provided in this Division" (a Division of the 2012 Act, not in the Act's text): the exception is
-- an input.
-- src:3598 | 210 Except as provided in this Division, PPP Canada Inc., incorporated under the Canada Business Corporations Act, is not an agent of Her Majesty in right of Canada.
@ref CBCA Related Provisions, S.C. 2012, c. 19, s. 210 (src:3598)
GIVEN `this Division of S.C. 2012, c. 19 provides that PPP Canada Inc. is an agent of Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `PPP Canada Inc. is an agent of Her Majesty in right of Canada within S.C. 2012, c. 19, s. 210` IF
    `this Division of S.C. 2012, c. 19 provides that PPP Canada Inc. is an agent of Her Majesty in right of Canada`
